<div class="px-4 sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
  <div class="sm:flex sm:items-center">
    <div class="sm:flex-auto">
      <h1 class="text-3xl font-semibold text-gray-900">Exercises</h1>
      <p class="mt-2 text-sm text-gray-700">Your movements and the built-in barbell library.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="mt-4 sm:ml-16 sm:mt-0 sm:flex-none">
      <a href="/exercises/new" class="<%= button_style %> block bg-lime-500 px-3 py-2 text-center text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900 hover:bg-lime-600">Add a new exercise</a>
    </div>
  </div>
  <div class="mt-8 flow-root">
    <div class="-mx-4 -my-2 overflow-x-auto sm:-mx-6 lg:-mx-8">
      <div class="inline-block min-w-full py-2 align-middle sm:px-6 lg:px-8">
        <table class="min-w-full divide-y divide-gray-300">
          <thead>
            <tr>
              <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3.5 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Name</th>
              <%# The training max, here because #411 takes the programme screens away and this
                  is where every movement is already listed. Percentages drive every main lift,
                  so "squat at 80%" is only meaningful beside the number it is 80% of.

                  Blank where nothing has been stated, rather than showing the derived reading:
                  a derived max is a reading off the sets and changes on its own, and a column
                  of them for fifty library movements nobody has trained would be noise around
                  the handful that are a standing instruction. The movement's own page still
                  shows the derived one, where there is room to say which kind it is. %>
              <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3.5 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Training max</th>
              <%# The rest, on the same argument as the training max beside it. #456.
                  The bell, the countdown and the column it counts to have all existed since
                  #281 and #395, and the bell has never rung for anybody: not one movement and
                  not one of 126 program lifts carries a rest. The app deliberately will not
                  invent one -- a countdown that rings unasked is the app deciding how long
                  somebody rests -- so the only way it ever rings is if a lifter names a
                  length, and nothing on any list showed that the question was there to answer.
                  A column of dashes is what makes an unanswered question look unanswered. %>
              <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3.5 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Rest</th>
              <th scope="col" class="px-3 py-3.5 text-left text-sm font-semibold text-gray-900">Source</th>
            </tr>
          </thead>
          <tbody class="divide-y divide-gray-200 bg-white">
            <%- @exercises.each do |exercise| %>
              <tr>
                <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-4 text-sm">
                  <a href="/exercises/<%= exercise[:id] %>"
                     class="font-medium text-lime-700 hover:text-lime-800"><%= exercise[:name] %></a>
                  <%- if provenance(exercise) %>
                    <div class="text-xs text-gray-500"><%= provenance(exercise) %></div>
                  <%- end %>
                </td>
                <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-4 text-sm">
                  <%- if (stated = @stated_maxes[exercise[:id]]) %>
                    <span class="font-medium tabular-nums text-gray-900"><%= weight_label(stated[:pounds]) %></span>
                    <span class="text-gray-500">lb</span>
                    <div class="text-xs text-gray-500">set <%= stated[:stated_at].strftime('%-d %b') %></div>
                  <%- else %>
                    <span class="text-gray-400">&mdash;</span>
                  <%- end %>
                </td>
                <%# Said through Timing.named, which is how the movement's own page and its
                    edit form both say it -- "180 seconds" and "3m" are the same fact, and two
                    spellings of it in one app is one too many.

                    `named` rather than `phrase`: this is a length a lifter typed, and phrase
                    drops the seconds above two minutes, so a rest of 150 read back as "2m" --
                    which is what 120 reads as too. Right for a measured turnaround, wrong for
                    somebody's own words. %>
                <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-4 text-sm">
                  <%- if (rest = @rests[exercise[:id]]) %>
                    <span class="font-medium tabular-nums text-gray-900">
                      <%= Tectonic::Timing.named(rest) %>
                    </span>
                  <%- else %>
                    <span class="text-gray-400">&mdash;</span>
                  <%- end %>
                </td>
                <td class="whitespace-nowrap px-3 py-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
                  <%= exercise.library? ? 'Library' : 'Yours' %>
                </td>
              </tr>
            <%- end %>
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
